1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,170
Whatcha doin' there?

2
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:08,100
Working on a new plan to catch the roadrunner?

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,240
The humorous implication being that I am Wile E. Coyote?

4
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:16,210
Yes.

5
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:18,780
And this is a schematic for a bird-trapping device

6
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:22,750
that will ultimately backfire and cause me physical injury?

7
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,020
Yes.

8
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:30,760
What I'm doing here

9
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:34,100
is trying to determine when I'm going to die.

10
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,600
A lot of people are working on that research.

11
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,340
So what is all this?

12
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:43,240
My family history factoring in longevity

13
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,640
propensity for disease, et cetera.

14
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,710
Interesting.

15
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,910
Cause of death for Uncle Carl was KBB.

16
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:49,950
What's "KBB"?

17
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:53,280
"Killed by badger."

18
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,020
How's that?

19
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:57,090
It was Thanksgiving.

20
00:00:57,090 --> 00:01:01,720
Uncle Carl said, "I think there's a badger living in our chimney. "

21
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,630
"Hand me that flashlight."

22
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:07,860
Those were the last words he ever spoke to us.

23
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,260
I don't think you need

24
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:12,270
to worry about death by badgers being hereditary.

25
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:13,740
Not true.

26
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,440
The fight or flight instinct is coded genetically.

27
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:20,440
Instead of fleeing, he chose to fight barehanded

28
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,110
against a brawny member of the weasel family.

29
00:01:23,110 --> 00:01:26,350
Who's to say that I don't share that flawed DNA?

30
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:28,920
You can always get a badger and find out.

31
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:34,560
But seriously

32
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,190
even if I disregard the Uncle Carl factor

33
00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:39,660
at best I have 60 years left.

34
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:42,260
That long, huh?

35
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:43,930
60 only takes me to here.

36
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:46,100
I need to get to here.

37
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,970
What's there?

38
00:01:47,970 --> 00:01:50,740
The earliest estimate of the singularity

39
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:52,970
when man will be able to transfer his consciousness

40
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,680
into machines and achieve immortality.

41
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:59,110
So, you're upset about missing out

42
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,820
on becoming some sort of freakish self-aware robot?

43
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:04,850
By this much.

44
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:08,120
Tough break.  You want eggs?

45
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,890
You don't get it, Leonard.

46
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:12,490
I'm going to miss so much.

47
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:18,030
the unified field theory, cold fusion, the dogapus.

48
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:19,630
What's a dogapus?

49
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:22,840
The hybrid dog and octopus.

50
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,810
Man's underwater best friend.

51
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:28,380
Is somebody working on that?

52
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,640
I was going to.

53
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:33,320
I planned on giving it to myself on my 300th birthday.

54
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,380
Wait a minute. You hate dogs.

55
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:38,720
A dogapus can play fetch with eight balls.

56
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,390
No one can hate that.

57
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,200
What do we owe you?

58
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,670
It came to $28.17.

59
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:11,800
Let's say six bucks apiece.

60
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,570
Here you go.

61
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:15,800
Thank you.

62
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,940
What?

63
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:22,240
Never mind. I got it.

64
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,780
Oh, you wanted me to pay.

65
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,010
- It's no big deal. - No, no, no, no. You're right.

66
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:28,450
We're not going out anymore; I should pay for myself.

67
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:32,420
What?

68
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,720
He said, "If he had woman parts

69
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,330
"he'd eat for free the rest of his life"

70
00:03:38,330 --> 00:03:41,500
Yeah, but you wouldn't be able to talk to yourself.

71
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:46,130
I'm a little low on cash.

72
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:48,240
- How much you got?  - Nothing.

73
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,770
How can you walk around with no money?

74
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,410
I'm cute. I get by.

75
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:53,170
It's okay, you can owe me.

76
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,410
- Thank you.  - Sheldon, six bucks.

77
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:58,180
No, thank you. I'm not eating pizza tonight.

78
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,280
But it's Thursday.

79
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,920
Thursday's pizza night.

80
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,020
Not for me.

81
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:05,090
Thursday is now Cruciferous Vegetable Night.

82
00:04:05,090 --> 00:04:08,460
Tonight's selection: Brussels sprouts.

83
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:09,590
Really?

84
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:12,290
You're changing the Sheldonian calendar?

85
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:15,400
- It's a small price to pay. - For what?

86
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,930
- No, no, don't ask. - Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.

87
00:04:17,930 --> 00:04:20,270
In order to live long enough to fuse my consciousness

88
00:04:20,270 --> 00:04:22,870
with cybernetics, I need to change my diet.

89
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:25,140
Wait. Cybernetics is robot stuff, right?

90
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,110
Correct.

91
00:04:26,110 --> 00:04:28,610
So you want to turn yourself into some sort of robot?

92
00:04:28,610 --> 00:04:30,810
Essentially, yes.

93
00:04:30,810 --> 00:04:32,080
Okay, here's my question.

94
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,510
Didn't you already do that?

95
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:38,490
Flattering, but sadly, no.

96
00:04:38,490 --> 00:04:41,960
I'm also planning to begin an exercise regimen

97
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:44,390
designed to strengthen my cardiovascular system.

98
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:46,660
AKA jogging.

99
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,230
Wait. Honey, have you ever run before?

100
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:49,530
Certainly.

101
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:53,740
I've run from bullies, dogs, angry chickens...

102
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:57,370
and one particularly persistent P.E. teacher

103
00:04:57,370 --> 00:05:00,640
determined to bend me over and give me a scoliosis test.

104
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:05,750
You're right. Penny jogs.

105
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:07,320
Maybe you guys can run together.

106
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,680
That's an excellent idea.

107
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,420
Yeah, if we chat

108
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,660
it will create the illusion of time going faster.

109
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:17,660
No, it won't.

110
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:20,900
Um, how does he know I jog?

111
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:25,170
Oh, he watches you from his car with high-powered binoculars.

112
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:27,040
Oh, my God, that is so creepy!

113
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,700
I know!

114
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:34,410
And he says he's not gonna stop.

115
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:41,050
Then see a shrink and figure out how to talk to women.

116
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:54,160
What the hell?

117
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:58,500
What's the matter?

118
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:01,540
I have pain radiating from my navel

119
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,370
to my lower right abdomen.

120
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:05,470
I'm nauseated and feverish.

121
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:08,340
I believe I may have cholera.

122
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:10,680
There's no cholera in Pasadena.

123
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:13,780
Just like last summer, when there was no malaria in Pasadena.

124
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:15,150
Well, if it's not cholera

125
00:06:15,150 --> 00:06:18,050
then based on a quick Internet search

126
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:20,920
the other explanations in decreasing order of likelihood

127
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:24,790
are Hirschsprung's Disease, botulism, a 30-foot tapeworm

128
00:06:24,790 --> 00:06:28,700
or accidental ingestion of chrysanthemum blossoms.

129
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:32,500
When would you have accidentally eaten chrysanthemum blossoms?

130
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,100
It's part of an unlikely scenario

131
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:36,740
that involves sleepwalking and a 24-hour flower mart

132
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:38,970
with a less-than- vigilant proprietor.

133
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:41,410
Oh, Lord, my belly!

134
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:43,280
Ever had your appendix out?

135
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,510
I haven't.

136
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:46,980
I've been meaning to, but who has the time?

137
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,550
Let's get you to the hospital.

138
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:53,750
So this is how it ends...

139
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,890
with cruel irony.

140
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:58,190
Just as I make the commitment to preserving my body

141
00:06:58,190 --> 00:07:01,730
I am betrayed by my appendix, a vestigial organ.

142
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:05,200
Do you know the original purpose of the appendix, Leonard?

143
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,300
No.

144
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:10,170
I do. And yet I'm doomed while you live on.

145
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:14,340
Funny how things work out, isn't it?

146
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:18,050
Oh, Lord, I think it's about to burst!

147
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:23,120
On the other hand

148
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,850
it might have been the Brussels sprouts.

149
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:29,390
Good night.

150
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:30,690
Good night.

151
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:32,290
Appendicitis.

152
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:35,000
What a nervous Nelly.

153
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:41,370
Penny! Penny! Penny!

154
00:07:41,370 --> 00:07:44,270
Coming, coming.

155
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:46,210
Hey, nice knees.

156
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:47,280
Thank you.

157
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,310
They're my mother's.

158
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:50,850
Oh. And the Flash shirt is what?

159
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:52,850
Because, what, you're gonna run really fast?

160
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:55,580
No, the Flash shirt is because it's Friday

161
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:58,050
but it's nice when things work out.

162
00:07:58,050 --> 00:08:00,150
- Where's your heart rate monitor?  - I don't have one.

163
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,920
- What about your pedometer?  - Don't have one.

164
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:04,460
Do you have telematics in your shoes connected to an iPod?

165
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,390
- Uh, no.  - What do you do

166
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:09,830
You just go out there and gambol about like a bunny?

167
00:08:09,830 --> 00:08:14,440
No. I just run till I'm hungry, then I stop for a bear claw.

168
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:19,170
Why are you doing that?

169
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,810
It's good to stretch your muscles before you run.

170
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:23,080
All right.

171
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,280
Let's start with a toe touch.

172
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:34,320
Okay, you do it.

173
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,290
I am doing it.

174
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,990
Oh. Wow. Good job.

175
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,930
Can you do this?

176
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:45,700
We'll never know.

177
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,000
Okay, let's just warm up on the run.

178
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,640
- Okay.  - Okay, let's go.

179
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,670
I've been reading up on biomechanics.

180
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,510
I think you'll be surprised at my...

181
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,050
Oh, my God, are you okay?

182
00:08:58,050 --> 00:08:59,180
I think so.

183
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,520
- Oh, let me help you up.  - Thank you.

184
00:09:03,850 --> 00:09:06,290
Oh, Sheldon!

185
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:08,290
If it makes you feel any better

186
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:11,790
Thursday is no longer Cruciferous Vegetable Night.

187
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,430
Here's my chicken curry.

188
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:16,830
Howard, your shrimp biryani.

189
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:18,930
- Thank you, sir.  - Palak paneer, that's Penny.

190
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:21,670
- Thanks.  - And for Rajesh Koothrappali

191
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:23,840
from whose homeland these tasty dishes originate

192
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:26,240
one large order of chicken McNuggets.

193
00:09:29,310 --> 00:09:31,610
- Hey, what's my share?  - Uh... 12 bucks.

194
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:34,150
- Okay, can I get you after Friday when I get paid?  - Sure.

195
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:35,880
What am I up to now?

196
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:38,220
Well, okay, with the Indian food, the pizza

197
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:40,250
the Thai food, the tank of gas

198
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,920
the frozen yogurt

199
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:44,230
and your rent, uh...

200
00:09:44,230 --> 00:09:47,090
a little over $1,400.

201
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,330
What now?

202
00:09:51,330 --> 00:09:53,300
He's just expressing his admiration that

203
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:57,100
you don't even have to put out to get free stuff.

204
00:09:59,710 --> 00:10:03,010
It's not free-- I'm gonna pay him back.

205
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:07,180
Shut up!

206
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,580
Sheldon, are you gonna join us?

207
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:11,150
Coming!

208
00:10:25,530 --> 00:10:27,740
Greetings, friends.

209
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:30,810
Greetings, whatever the hell you are.

210
00:10:30,810 --> 00:10:34,210
I am a mobile virtual presence device.

211
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,810
Recent events

212
00:10:35,810 --> 00:10:39,250
have demonstrated to me that my body is too fragile

213
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:41,750
to endure the vicissitudes of the world.

214
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:44,220
Until such time as I am able

215
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,650
to transfer my consciousness

216
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:48,490
I shall remain in a secure location

217
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:51,830
and interact with the world in this manner.

218
00:10:52,630 --> 00:10:54,030
Really? That's your question--

219
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:56,560
when did he put a ramp in?

220
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,840
You're in my spot.

221
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:20,730
This may seem a little odd at first

222
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:23,370
but over time, you'll grow accustomed

223
00:11:23,370 --> 00:11:26,670
to dealing with me in this configuration.

224
00:11:26,670 --> 00:11:29,570
Yeah, to be honest, I don't see much difference.

225
00:11:29,570 --> 00:11:30,770
Thank you.

226
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:32,980
That's what I was going for.

227
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:37,680
Now, Leonard, tomorrow, when we go to work

228
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,650
you'll need to allow some extra time

229
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:41,450
to get me down the stairs.

230
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:46,120
For your convenience, I disassemble into four pieces.

231
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,160
This is ridiculous.

232
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:48,330
I'm coming to talk to you.

233
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:50,630
You don't know where I am.

234
00:11:52,030 --> 00:11:54,670
My physical body is safely ensconced

235
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:57,370
in a secure, undisclosed location.

236
00:11:57,370 --> 00:11:58,970
You're in your bedroom.

237
00:11:58,970 --> 00:12:00,570
No, I'm not.

238
00:12:00,570 --> 00:12:03,910
I can hear your voice coming from your bedroom.

239
00:12:05,110 --> 00:12:07,240
No, you can't.

240
00:12:09,310 --> 00:12:10,580
Wait.

241
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,950
Come back.

242
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:13,220
Halt.

243
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:16,620
Authorized personnel only!

244
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,090
So, either one of you weirdos

245
00:12:19,090 --> 00:12:22,090
want to buy my underwear? Only 1,400 bucks.

246
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,600
Sheldon, this is ridiculous.

247
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,170
I'm behind you.

248
00:12:30,170 --> 00:12:33,370
Please look at me when you're talking to me.

249
00:12:33,370 --> 00:12:34,870
I am looking at you.

250
00:12:34,870 --> 00:12:36,170
No, you're not.

251
00:12:36,170 --> 00:12:38,640
Pay no attention to that man in the bed.

252
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:41,680
You cannot exist as a virtual presence.

253
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,550
Not here and certainly not at work.

254
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:45,420
Oh, good God.

255
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:47,020
At my age, do you know

256
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:49,850
how I'm statistically most likely to die?

257
00:12:49,850 --> 00:12:52,120
At the hands of your roommate?

258
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,690
An accident.

259
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:56,160
That's how I'm going to make it look.

260
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:58,800
Until I can transfer my intellect

261
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,100
to a more durable container

262
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:02,870
my body will remain safely ensconced in my bed.

263
00:13:02,870 --> 00:13:04,940
Fine, but don't expect my help.

264
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:07,500
You have to help-- it's in the roommate agreement.

265
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:09,010
No, it's not.

266
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:13,340
Section 74.C.

267
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,850
The various obligations and duties of the parties

268
00:13:15,850 --> 00:13:19,480
in the event one of them becomes a robot.

269
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:23,150
I'll be damned.

270
00:13:33,530 --> 00:13:35,330
This is delightful.

271
00:13:35,330 --> 00:13:37,330
Uh-huh.

272
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:39,600
It's much easier to enjoy

273
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,610
the picturesque route we travel to work

274
00:13:41,610 --> 00:13:44,840
when you remove the specter of fiery vehicular death.

275
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,110
Refresh my memory.

276
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:48,710
Why didn't I just put you in the trunk?

277
00:13:48,710 --> 00:13:51,680
Because I called shotgun. Remember?

278
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:54,350
Right.

279
00:13:57,990 --> 00:14:00,690
You seem tense.

280
00:14:00,690 --> 00:14:03,390
Perhaps this will relax you.

281
00:14:12,670 --> 00:14:14,540
I don't want to listen to music, Sheldon.

282
00:14:16,770 --> 00:14:18,140
Very well.

283
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:22,050
I don't understand why you're not enjoying this.

284
00:14:22,050 --> 00:14:26,580
Together, in this car, with my enhanced capabilities

285
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:29,120
we're like Knight Rider.

286
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:32,920
Except in Knight Rider, the car isn't a yammering sphincter.

287
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:35,860
You mock the sphincter

288
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:38,630
but the sphincter is a class of muscle

289
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:41,100
without which human beings couldn't survive.

290
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:46,440
There are over 50 different sphincters

291
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,110
in the human body.

292
00:14:48,110 --> 00:14:50,470
How many can you name?

293
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:54,380
I was wrong-- this is exactly like Knight Rider.

294
00:14:55,510 --> 00:14:57,510
Perhaps you'd be interested in a different game.

295
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:58,980
No.

296
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,580
This is a photograph of the 1911

297
00:15:00,590 --> 00:15:03,990
Solvay Conference on the theory of radiation and quanta.

298
00:15:03,990 --> 00:15:08,490
Using Photoshop, I've introduced a few anachronisms.

299
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,860
See if you can spot all 24.

300
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:12,360
I'll give you the first one.

301
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:16,670
Madame Curie should not be wearing a digital watch.

302
00:15:16,670 --> 00:15:18,040
And go.

303
00:15:20,470 --> 00:15:22,070
That's it. Bye-bye.

304
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:27,040
Bazinga.

305
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,450
I have an override switch.

306
00:15:31,450 --> 00:15:33,050
I almost died!

307
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:35,550
And I'm safe and sound in bed.

308
00:15:35,550 --> 00:15:37,720
Who's crazy now?

309
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:40,420
I'm still going to go with you.

310
00:15:46,330 --> 00:15:48,430
Hello, Professor Hoskins.

311
00:15:48,430 --> 00:15:51,170
Nice to see you, Mindy.

312
00:15:51,170 --> 00:15:53,970
And konnichiwa, Dr. Nakamura.

313
00:15:53,970 --> 00:15:57,610
Sorry the Swedes disproved your theory.

314
00:16:04,650 --> 00:16:06,650
Leonard, my door.

315
00:16:06,650 --> 00:16:07,880
What about it?

316
00:16:07,890 --> 00:16:10,720
Be a lamb and open it for me.

317
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,660
Why? What's the problem?

318
00:16:18,530 --> 00:16:21,470
You think you have me stymied, don't you?

319
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:24,940
No, I think a doorknob has you stymied.

320
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:29,510
Oh, look, it's Leonard and R2-D-Bag.

321
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:33,010
That's my joke. I told it last night.

322
00:16:33,010 --> 00:16:35,280
You can't just use it.

323
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:38,680
Raj, be a lamb and open the door for me.

324
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:41,250
Oh, sure.

325
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:45,060
He's a lamb.

326
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:46,860
You're not.

327
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,460
I'm a lamb.

328
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:55,570
Isn't this nice?

329
00:16:55,570 --> 00:16:58,840
The pleasures of fellowship and camaraderie

330
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:02,970
without having to tolerate your germy breath on my skin.

331
00:17:02,970 --> 00:17:05,080
I say we just take him to Tatooine

332
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:07,040
and sell him to some Jawas.

333
00:17:07,050 --> 00:17:08,710
That's two, dude.

334
00:17:08,710 --> 00:17:10,450
Write your own jokes.

335
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:13,580
Oh, great.

336
00:17:15,350 --> 00:17:17,250
Hi, I'm Penny, I'll be your waitress.

337
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,890
Why are you introducing yourself?

338
00:17:18,890 --> 00:17:20,060
I'd rather people not know

339
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:22,590
I have any prior connection to you whatsoever.

340
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,760
Can you tell me the specials this evening?

341
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,260
Sheldon, I'm not waiting on you.

342
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:28,230
Obviously.

343
00:17:28,230 --> 00:17:30,470
I don't even have water yet.

344
00:17:30,470 --> 00:17:32,040
Because you're not here.

345
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:35,470
That's discrimination against the otherwise located.

346
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:38,410
I'm going to have to go over your head.

347
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:44,210
Manager... manager.

348
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:47,950
Oh, Lord, look who it is.

349
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:51,120
Is that Steve Wozniak?

350
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,020
I think it is.

351
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:54,760
The Great and Powerful Woz.

352
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:56,630
Penny, Steve Wozniak was

353
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:58,800
one of the cofounders of Apple Computer.

354
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,230
- He and Steve Jobs started it...  - Yeah

355
00:18:00,230 --> 00:18:02,370
I know who he is. I watch Dancing with the Stars.

356
00:18:03,430 --> 00:18:05,440
I must speak to him.

357
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,840
Of course you must.

358
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:11,540
You know, there's an Olive Garden down the street.

359
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:14,110
You guys should try it sometime.

360
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:17,080
Excuse me, Mr. Wozniak?

361
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,250
Oh, hey.

362
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:20,150
Nice virtual presence device.

363
00:18:20,150 --> 00:18:21,150
Thank you.

364
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:23,720
I just want to say I'm a big fan.

365
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:27,620
You're my 15th favorite technological visionary.

366
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:29,290
Only 15th?

367
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:32,900
It's still six spots above Steve Jobs.

368
00:18:33,830 --> 00:18:37,100
I care neither for turtlenecks nor showmanship.

369
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:40,470
Yeah, I never got that turtleneck thing.

370
00:18:40,470 --> 00:18:44,410
One of my proudest possessions is a vintage 1977 Apple Two.

371
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:48,950
Despite the file system limitations of Apple DOS 3.3

372
00:18:48,950 --> 00:18:51,250
it was a pretty nifty little achievement.

373
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:53,520
Thanks, we were shooting for "nifty."

374
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:55,390
You know, if you had it here

375
00:18:55,390 --> 00:18:56,990
I'd autograph it for you.

376
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:00,220
Don't move for 15 to 30 minutes

377
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:02,930
depending on how the buses are running.

378
00:19:04,730 --> 00:19:07,200
Nerds.

379
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:12,600
I'm coming, Woz, I'm coming.

380
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:37,950
Penny... Penny... Penny.

381
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:40,950
What up, Shel-Bot?

382
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:42,820
I can't get out of bed.

383
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,190
I hurt my ankle.

384
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,790
What do you want me to do?

385
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:48,120
Sing me "Soft Kitty."

386
00:19:48,130 --> 00:19:50,830
Really, you want me to sing "Soft Kitty"

387
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:52,460
to a computer monitor?

388
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,300
Would you rather come over and sing it to me in person?

389
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:58,570
Soft kitty, warm kitty

390
00:19:58,570 --> 00:20:00,470
Little ball of fur...

391
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:03,070
Closer to the microphone.

392
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:06,380
Happy kitty, sleepy...

393
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,650
No.

394
00:20:08,650 --> 00:20:11,920
You have to start over.

395
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:15,250
Soft kitty, warm kitty

396
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:18,390
Little ball of fur

397
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:21,190
Happy kitty, sleepy kitty

398
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:24,160
Purr, purr, purr.

